   "text": "I built an 8-cube chain, 167 x 20 x 20 mm, as one watertight part on a new plate. The 20 mm cubes are joined by 0.6 mm living hinges, with the hinge line alternating between the top edge and the front edge so the chain can fold in more than one direction.\n\nThis is not a true infinity cube yet. It is an open chain, not a closed loop, and the hinges are thin flexure strips rather than pin hinges with print-in-place clearance, which my tools can't subtract. PLA will likely crack at the strips after many folds, so PETG or TPU would last longer.\n\nI haven't sliced or queued it. Do you want me to slice it for your P1S, or would you rather change the hinge design first?"
